Gap: `h_msg`'s `out.as_chunks_mut::<32>().0.iter_mut().enumerate()`, and `Iterator::sum` in `path_range`, `OtsKey::of_index` and `codeword` - Lean rejects the translation: the hax Lean library has no `Iterator` for `IterMut`, no `as_chunks_mut`, and no `Iterator::sum`
Each becomes a loop by index.
`h_msg`: call `i`'s digest goes to bytes `32i..32(i + 1)` for `i < DIGEST_CALLS`, which is the
chunks of `out` in order.
`path_range` and `OtsKey::of_index`: `LAYER_HEIGHTS[..layer].iter().sum()` is the sum of
`LAYER_HEIGHTS[l]` for `l < layer`.
`codeword`: the sum of the chunks `x[i] as usize` for `i < V`. Additions in the same order, none
of which can overflow (at most `3 * V`).
Tests: each against the expression copied from the source.
h_msg_by_index_matches_the_chunks (no branches), on four inputs;
path_range_by_index_matches_the_sum and of_index_by_index_matches_the_sum (no branches), on every
layer, so with none, one and two layers below, the second at nine indices;
codeword_by_index_matches_the_iterator: four digests whose chunks sum to `T`, with every chunk
value among them (`Some`), each with its first or last chunk changed (`None`), and four other
digests (`None`).
mutation: `h_msg`'s first call skipped (`1..DIGEST_CALLS`) -> it fails; `path_range`'s sum from
layer 1 (`1..layer`) -> it fails; `of_index`'s sum from layer 1 -> it fails; `codeword`'s sum from
chunk 1 (`1..V`) -> it fails. Each fails its own test.

